Debian 11 "bullseye" standard container template for s390x
==========================================================

Unofficial build of the Proxmox-390 project (https://proxmox-390.legitimatebusiness.be).
Not produced, endorsed or supported by Proxmox Server Solutions GmbH.

Same definition as archive/debian-11-bullseye-std-64 (the last upstream
Debian 11 appliance), built for s390x. dab.conf differs in Architecture,
Version, Maintainer, Description and Source; the Makefile excludes s390-tools
and sysconfig-hardware (pulled in by priority on s390x only, useless in a
container without CCW hardware). Without them the package list equals the
amd64 debian-11-standard_11.7-1 template, minus dmidecode (not built for s390x).

End of life: Debian 11 is only maintained by Debian LTS, which does not cover
s390x. deb.debian.org no longer carries bullseye for s390x, so the sources
point at archive.debian.org (bullseye, the final 11.11 point release, and
bullseye-updates). There are no security updates. archive.debian.org's
Release files carry no Valid-Until, so apt works without extra options.
Use debian-13-standard for anything that needs security support.

Requirements
------------
- dab with s390x support: https://github.com/Proxmox-390/dab, branch
  s390x/packaging (allows Architecture: s390x).
- An s390x host or VM running Debian 13 with lxc-pve (or lxc) and xz-utils
  installed: dab runs the target's binaries in an LXC container, so it cannot
  cross-build.

Build
-----
  make            # -> debian-11-standard_11.11-1_s390x.tar.zst

dab writes its Source: lines into the template's /etc/apt/sources.list, so
keep the archive.debian.org lines for a release build. To download through a
local mirror or proxy instead, add a Mirror: line to dab.conf, e.g.

  Mirror: http://archive.debian.org/debian => http://mirror.example.com/debian-archive

Mirrors are only used for downloads and never end up in the template.

Published
---------
Built templates are published in the Proxmox-390 container template index,
https://proxmox-390-apt.legitimatebusiness.be/container-index/, which pveam
on Proxmox-390 nodes uses (signed with the Proxmox-390 archive key).
